== Heraldry ==

=== Coat of arms ===

''' [[Blazon]] '''
[[File:313 MI Bn Coat of Arms.png|thumb|125px|right|Coat of arms]]

The coat of arms features an [[Azure (heraldry)|Azure]] (teal blue) [[Escutcheon (heraldry)|shield]] with an [[Ordinary (heraldry)|ordinary]] of an [[Argent]] (white) and [[Tenné]] (orange) [[Check (pattern)|checkered]] [[fess]]. The [[Charge (heraldry)|charge]] of the shield is an Argent six-pointed [[Star (heraldry)|mullet]] of the second. Atop the shield rests an Argent and Azure [[Torse|rolled wreath]] which forms the base of the [[Crest (heraldry)|crest]] featuring a [[Gules]] (red) [[Enfield (heraldry)|dragon]] trimmed in [[Or (heraldry)|Or]] (gold) in a [[Attitude (heraldry)#Passant|passant]] posture. The dragon stands in front of a [[Vert (heraldry)|Vert]] (green) [[Mount (heraldry)|mountain]] which is impaled with twelve [[Tincture (heraldry)#Proper|Proper]] [[bamboo]] spikes while the dragon's tail is interlaced through the spikes.

''' Symbolism '''

Azure and white are the colors used for units not assigned to a [[Structure of the United States Army#Branches and functional areas|branch]], referring to the unit's previous designation as the 313th ASA Battalion. The colors orange and white express the organization's former affiliation with the Signal Corps and the six points of the mullet allude to the battalion's decorations for World War II and Vietnam service.. The dragon symbolizes alertness and readiness, and its [[Chinese dragon|Asian styling]] denotes the unit's service in Vietnam. The green mountain represents the lush vegetation and [[Annamite Range|mountainous terrain]] while the twelve bamboo spikes represent the twelve campaigns the battalion participated in during the Vietnam war.<ref name=TIOH1 />

=== Distinctive unit insignia ===

''' Blazon '''
[[File:313_MI_Flash_with_DUI_and_Oval_with_JM_Badge.png|thumb|right|250px|Flash with DUI ''(left)'' and background oval with master parachutist badge ''(right)'']]

The unit's distinctive unit insignia (DUI) is a silver color metal and enamel device {{convert|1+1/8|in|cm}} in height overall consisting of a shield representing the unit's coat of arms with a silver [[Scroll (art)|scroll]] attached around the sides and bottom of the shield inscribed, "SAVOIR C'EST POUVOIR" (''Knowledge is power'', in French) with [[Sable (heraldry)|black]]-colored lettering.<ref name=TIOH1>[https://web.archive.org/web/20241030151501/https://tioh.army.mil/Catalog/HeraldryMulti.aspx?CategoryId=3869&grp=2&menu=Uniformed%20Services Distinctive Unit Insignia and Coat of Arms of the 313th Military Intelligence Battalion.] Retrieved from [[United States Army Institute of Heraldry|The Institute of Heraldry]] on 11 August 2020.</ref>

=== Beret flash and background trimming ===

The 313th's flash is a teal blue shield-shaped embroidered item with a semi-circular base. Around the edge of the flash is a {{convert|1/8|in|cm}} orange border, two white lightning bolts [[Bend (heraldry)#Bend sinister|bendwise sinister]], one issuing from the top of the flash and one issuing from the lower right side; the overall dimensions are {{convert|2+1/4|in|cm}} in height by {{convert|1+7/8|in|cm}} in width. The airborne background trimming is a teal blue oval-shaped embroidered item edged with a {{convert|1/8|in|cm}} orange border two white lightning bolts bendwise sinister, one issuing from the top of the item and one issuing from the right side. The overall dimensions are {{convert|1+3/8|in|cm}} in height by {{convert|2+1/4|in|cm}} width.<ref name=TIOH2>[https://web.archive.org/web/20231126001947/https://tioh.army.mil/Catalog/HeraldryMulti.aspx?CategoryId=4938&grp=2&menu=Uniformed%20Services Beret Flash and Background Trimming of the 313th Military Intelligence Battalion.] Retrieved from The Institute of Heraldry on 11 August 2020.</ref>

